Changelog: 15-10-2026 23:29:43

Release 0.1.21.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:51:19

Release 0.1.21.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:04:04

Bazzite's update state (owner's decision 15-10-2026, an exception to the suite's scope rule): a Bazzite card on top
(bazzite.py) shows the running image with its build date, an update installed and waiting for a reboot (Reboot to
update; a rollback is not taken for one), and uupd's last run, warning when it failed or has not run for over a week.
It only reads, from rpm-ostree status --json and systemctl show, without root or the network. A weekly reminder:
--bazzite-reminder shows no window and gives a desktop notification (notify-send) only when an update waits or the
updater failed or stopped; install.sh writes the systemd user units bc250-bazzite-update-reminder.service and .timer
(Mondays 10:00, Persistent, so a missed Monday is caught up at the next login) and enables them (without a user
session by the enable link itself), and --uninstall stops and removes them. The portal, README and wiki summaries
mention it. Tests: tests/test_bazzite.py (the owner's board's recorded state, an update waiting, a rollback, the
updater failed, stale or never run, no rpm-ostree, only read commands, the notification, the entry point) and the card
in test_window.py; the installer test covers the units, enabling with and without a session, and the removal.

